CEO Summary
Provides a secure identity API for account registration, identity lookup, challenge authentication, and JWT sessions.

Uses public-key authentication, so private user keys never leave the client application or reach the server.

Protects authenticated operations by validating JWT signatures, issuer, and expiration.

Limits abuse with rate limits on registration, challenge requests, authentication attempts, and overall API traffic.

Keeps the backend private, with Rust listening only on 127.0.0.1:8080.

Exposes only HTTPS publicly through Caddy on port 443, with automatic TLS certificate management.

Provides operational visibility through structured API access logs containing endpoint, status, latency, timestamp, and request ID.

Creates API usage reports showing request volume by endpoint in 15-minute time buckets, with CSV, JSON, and HTML visualizations.

Creates security oversight reports covering service health, SSM activity, login activity, failed services, package history, open ports, disk, and memory.

Protects operational data by uploading reports to encrypted S3 storage and automatically deleting local logs older than 14 days.

The result is a small, cost-conscious identity platform with authentication, abuse controls, HTTPS protection, operational monitoring, usage analytics, and recoverable AWS-based administration.